1
00:00:00,362 --> 00:00:05,469
System administration — Roles and permissions, company settings, backups and the audit log — for the CEO and Operations.

2
00:00:07,197 --> 00:00:12,802
System administration is behind the gear in the top bar. Only the CEO and Operations managers see it.

3
00:00:17,403 --> 00:00:24,906
Roles &amp; permissions: what each of the nine roles may do. Y is allowed, T for their own team, P for their own projects, – not allowed.

4
00:00:25,642 --> 00:00:28,867
Each person's role is set on Management → People.

5
00:00:29,637 --> 00:00:36,261
Company settings: the daily and weekly hour limits, the default contract hours, and the month-end close that locks a month for payroll.

6
00:00:39,217 --> 00:00:43,250
Changes here apply to everyone, from the next entry on.

7
00:00:44,032 --> 00:00:49,635
Backup &amp; restore: download all of WorkDesk's data as one file, and bring it back if ever needed.

8
00:00:52,538 --> 00:00:57,559
The data is also saved automatically after every change — this is for an extra copy you keep yourself.

9
00:00:58,332 --> 00:01:03,189
The Audit log records every change: who did what, when, and what it was before.

10
00:01:06,211 --> 00:01:10,218
Search and filter it to answer "who changed this?" in seconds.

11
00:01:12,914 --> 00:01:17,022
Roles · settings · backups · audit — More help: the Handbook → System administration.
